  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Partnership to Counter Migrant Smuggling and Human Trafficking Along the Central Mediterranean Route -PARCOURS</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Algeria has seen in recent years a surge in the entry of irregular migrants. Some of these migrants resort to the services of criminal smuggling networks, while others are victims of human trafficking. In response to this situation, IOM proposes a project to contribute to counter migrant smuggling and human trafficking along the Central Mediterranean Route. In particular, the project seeks to promote a coherent and multi-disciplinary response to migrant smuggling and human trafficking, involving close co-ordination between relevant stakeholders at international, regional and national level, to support law enforcement efforts and ensure that appropriate assistance is available to migrants in need.</narrative>
  </description>
